@startuml view-3
title View 3 - Who depends on the persisted data (layers and entity access)
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Boundary (Swing GUIs)" {
  [UserRegistrationGUI] as G1
  [UserLoginGUI] as G2
  [ReportCreationGUI] as G3
  [SubmittedReportsGUI] as G4
  [ReceivedReportsGUI] as G5
  [ReportStatusUpdateGUI] as G6
  [InternalNoteGUI] as G7
  [ActivityMonitoringGUI] as G8
}

package "Control" {
  [SystemServicesController\n(facade)] as SSC
  [UserLoginController] as C_login
  [UserRegistrationController] as C_reg
  [ReportCreationController] as C_create
  [ReportReviewController] as C_review
  [ReportDetailsController] as C_det
  [ReportStatusUpdateController] as C_status
  [NotificationController] as C_notif
  [InternalNoteController] as C_note
  [ActivityMonitoringController] as C_mon
}

package "Entity (domain + services)" {
  [UserService] as US
  [ReportService] as RS
  [User / Citizen /\nMunicipalOperator] as EU
  [Report\n(+ Location, ReportCategory,\nReportStatus states)] as ER
  [StatusUpdate] as ESU
  [InternalNote] as EIN
  [Notification] as ENO
}

package "Database" {
  [PersistenceService\nsave / update / findById /\nfindByFields / findByAttribute] as PS
  [JpaUtil\n(EntityManagerFactory)] as JU
}
database "MySQL reports_db\nusers, reports, status_updates,\ninternal_notes, notifications" as DB

G1 --> SSC
G3 --> SSC
G4 --> SSC
G5 --> SSC
G6 --> SSC
G7 --> SSC
G8 --> SSC
G2 --> C_login

SSC --> C_reg
SSC --> C_create
SSC --> C_review
SSC --> C_det
SSC --> C_status
SSC --> C_note
SSC --> C_mon
C_status --> C_notif

C_login --> US
C_reg --> US
C_create --> US
C_create --> RS
C_review --> US
C_review --> RS
C_det --> US
C_det --> RS
C_status --> US
C_status --> RS
C_note --> US
C_note --> RS
C_mon --> US
C_mon --> RS
C_notif --> RS

US --> PS
RS --> PS
US ..> EU : read/write users
RS ..> ER : read/write reports
ER *-- ESU : cascade
ER *-- EIN : cascade
RS ..> ENO : save / query by report
RS ..> ESU : query history
RS ..> EIN : query notes
PS --> JU
JU --> DB : JPA/Hibernate (persistence.xml)

note bottom of RS
  Data operations by use case (ReportService / UserService)
  - register user: INSERT users; check email uniqueness (credentials.email)
  - login: SELECT users by credentials.email + password
  - create report: INSERT reports (citizen from users)
  - sent reports: reports WHERE citizenReporting.userId
  - received reports / monitoring: reports WHERE category, location.municipalArea,
    currentStatusName (+ date range and counts computed in Java on report_date)
  - details: reports + notifications + internal_notes by report.reportId
  - history: status_updates by report.reportId
  - update status: MERGE reports (+ new status_updates row)
  - add note: MERGE reports (+ new internal_notes row)
  - notify: INSERT notifications for the reporting citizen
end note

note bottom of PS
  Queries are built as JPQL from attribute-name strings
  (e.g. "citizenReporting.userId", "location.municipalArea",
  "currentStatusName", "credentials.email").
  Renaming entity fields or columns breaks callers at runtime, not compile time.
end note
@enduml
